WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Welcome to the Man of Recaps. You may have noticed&nbsp;
a lot of these new Star Wars series are bringing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.000
into live action characters that were introduced&nbsp;
in the animated Clone Wars or Rebels. If you love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Star Wars, they're both great and you should&nbsp;
watch them. But if you don't have the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;I got you covered.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.360
To start you off with&nbsp;
the super simplified Star Wars timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.520
the Galaxy went Republic,&nbsp;
Empire, Republic, Empire.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.660
The Clone Wars takes place here, in between&nbsp;
Episodes Two and Three. Remember the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.980
was in a civil war between the Republic and&nbsp;
the Separatist Alliance. It stars our Jedi main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.000
characters from the prequel movies, Anakin&nbsp;
Skywalker and his master, Obi-Wan Kenobi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.080
The Jedi are generals in this war, leading the&nbsp;
Republic forces against the separatist Droid army.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.280
And remember, it's called the Clone Wars because&nbsp;
the Republic troops are all clones. But right at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.660
the start we're introduced to a new main character&nbsp;
who wasn't in the movies, the young Jedi Padawan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:48.120
Ahsoka Tano, who's been assigned to Anakin as an&nbsp;
apprentice. She's real fun, calls him Sky Guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.600
"Oh, don't get snippy with me, Snips!" And&nbsp;
pretty soon these two are best friends.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.080
But Anakin's not the only one who had an&nbsp;
apprentice that wasn't in the movies. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.380
Separatist leader, Count Dooku, is&nbsp;
training the skinny goth assassin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.360
Asajj Ventress. She's real cool, fights with&nbsp;
two lightsabers, and eventually Ahsoka does too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.420
because I mean two sabers are better&nbsp;
than one. So the show features all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.540
the big characters from the prequel&nbsp;
movies: Yoda, Mace Windu, Count Dooku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.300
General Grievous, but it also sometimes&nbsp;
features some of the background characters.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.540
That's why, if you ask a Star Wars&nbsp;
super-fan who their favorite Jedi is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.620
they're saying someone you've never heard of,&nbsp;
like Plo Koon. Padme Amidala has a pretty big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.520
role as the senator for Naboo, and remember,&nbsp;
she and Anakin are secretly married. She goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.180
out on diplomatic missions, but diplomacy&nbsp;
usually fails, and she has to resort to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.780
aggressive diplomacy. And, of course, there's&nbsp;
Chancellor Palpatine, leader of the Republic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:36.600
but secretly he's leader of the separatists&nbsp;
too, as his Sith alter ego, Darth Sidious!

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.720
A major new character introduced&nbsp;
in the show is the lovable pirate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.720
Hondo Ohnaka. The Jedi sometimes&nbsp;
work with him on smuggling stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.320
but Hondo is always willing to betray him if he&nbsp;
can make a bigger profit. But the separatists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.140
can't really be trusted to pay him, so most&nbsp;
of the time he's working for the Republic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:55.380
as a good-ish guy. But on the flipside is bounty&nbsp;
hunter Cad Bane, who has just a really cool hat.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.680
He's a bad dude that's a cold blooded&nbsp;
killer, and he's a great fighter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.000
he can hang with these Jedi. Speaking of bounty&nbsp;
hunters, there's a young Boba Fett who's formed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.300
his own little bounty hunter crew. He tries&nbsp;
to get revenge on Mace Windu, who remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.680
killed his father Jango Fett in Attack of the&nbsp;
Clones. On Onderon we meet a young Saw Gerrera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.560
who would go on to be a somewhat brutal&nbsp;
rebel leader featured in Rogue One.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.260
And of course, some of the main&nbsp;
characters in the Clone Wars are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.200
the Clone Troopers themselves. Yeah,&nbsp;
they may all be genetically identical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.440
but they all have their own personalities.&nbsp;
The main one we follow is Captain Rex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.800
who's in charge of Anakin's Division the&nbsp;
501st. They're all born with numbers, but they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.000
get nicknames like "Echo" who repeats things, or&nbsp;
sometimes just "Fives," whose number is all fives.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.900
The main theme of the Clone Wars is that these&nbsp;
troopers aren't expendable machines like droids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.920
they're real people. This comes to a head when&nbsp;
the 501st is lent out to the Jedi General Krell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.640
who treats them like they are disposable,&nbsp;
sends them into suicide missions. It's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.520
intense military dilemma, do you trust your&nbsp;
commanding officer sees the big picture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.920
or do you have to disobey orders&nbsp;
when they're clearly incompetent?

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.640
But in the end, they realize he's used the cover&nbsp;
of darkness to have the clones fight themselves!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.240
Yes he's actively turned to the Dark Side,&nbsp;
betrayed the republic to join the separatists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.840
so the clones put him down. But the most&nbsp;
important arc begins with Asajj Ventress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.780
Remember, the Sith have a Rule of&nbsp;
Two: one master, one apprentice.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.080
Because if the apprentice takes an apprentice,&nbsp;
they can team up and overthrow the master. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.720
Dooku tries to have Ventress killed,&nbsp;
but she escapes and goes back to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.080
home planet ruled by the Night Mother, a&nbsp;
powerful witch. She helps to get revenge on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.280
Dooku by buffing up one of the males of their&nbsp;
species, this absolute beast, Savage Oppress.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.820
He and Ventress team up to go kill Dooku,&nbsp;
but it doesn't work, Dooku's too strong. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:21.180
Ventress goes off to find new meaning in her&nbsp;
life, She briefly joins Boba Fett's group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.240
bounty hunters. But the Night Mother has a&nbsp;
new plan for revenge with the strongest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.740
their species, yes, it's Darth Maul! A super&nbsp;
cool villain that was underused in the movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.100
because he died at the end of Episode&nbsp;
One when Obi-Wan Kenobi cut him in half.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.420
But turns out he's a hard guy to kill. He&nbsp;
survived with just the top half of his body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.440
grafted onto spider droid legs! The night&nbsp;
Mother hooks him up with a new pair of legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:44.640
and yes it's happening, Darth Maul&nbsp;
is back! His primary goal is revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.940
on Obi Wan Kenobi, he and Savage fight&nbsp;
him a bunch, but they can't beat him.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:52.740
So now let's cut over to the planet of Mandalore.&nbsp;
Yes, the people with the super cool armor that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

