00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.400
He manipulates Ezra to use the Sith&nbsp;
Holicron to activate the temple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:05.160
which is a big weapon. Then Maul will&nbsp;
make Ezra his new Dark Side apprentice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.120
and together they'll overthrow the Emperor&nbsp;
and rule the galaxy. But Kanan Jarrus isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.200
going to let that happen. Yes he's been blinded,&nbsp;
but he gets lucky and throws Darth Maul off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:18.060
cliff. But someone noticed when they activated&nbsp;
the temple - oh, snap! It's Darth Vader.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:20.100
And this became an iconic Vader line:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:26.280
"I'm not afraid of you!" "Then you will die&nbsp;
braver than most." But now Ahsoka Tano arrives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:32.340
and it's time for the epic master apprentice&nbsp;
lightsaber duel! But when she cuts open his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:36.060
mask she gets to see it really is her&nbsp;
old friend and mentor Anakin in there.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:41.340
But at this point Darth Vader has fully&nbsp;
disassociated, "I killed Anakin Skywalker."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.300
So as Ezra and Kanan deactivate the temple,&nbsp;
Ahsoka stays behind to finish off Vader.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.920
But when we see Vader walking away, Ahsoka&nbsp;
Tano is presumed dead. So the rebels have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.040
been searching for a new home base, and of&nbsp;
course it's Chopper who finds one for them.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.840
He befriends an Imperial Droid, AP-5, who&nbsp;
becomes his sassy C-3PO to Chopper's R2-D2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.260
He helps them find the planet Atollon, not&nbsp;
on imperial charts. And it's a pretty great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:05.760
base except for the giant spider monsters. Now&nbsp;
Kanan Jarrus is permanently blind, but he finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.960
a mystic creature Bendu who teaches them how&nbsp;
to see through the Force. Now Ezra Bridger has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:14.040
buzzed his hair and built himself a new green&nbsp;
light saber, he's becoming a real strong Jedi.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:18.300
But he started playing with the Sith Holocron,&nbsp;
and flirting with the Dark Side! But pretty soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:22.140
Kanan helps him realize the Dark Side is bad.&nbsp;
But now Maul comes back to get that Holocron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:26.100
and he makes Ezra open up a Jedi one with it,&nbsp;
which combined will answer any question you want.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:31.860
And the question Maul most wanted answered is&nbsp;
the location of his old rival, Obi-Wan Kenobi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:37.080
And so it's time for the final old man Obi-Wan&nbsp;
Darth Maul duel! But as soon as it starts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:42.180
it's already over. Yes, Obi-Wan's been ready for&nbsp;
this, takes him out in one blow, samurai style.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:46.140
And it is kind of a sad moment as Obi-Wan&nbsp;
just pities Maul, he never had a chance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.980
was brought to the dark side at a young age,&nbsp;
and lived a life of pain and anger. So now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.100
we know how Maul's story ends, but this&nbsp;
probably isn't the last we'll see of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.860
because he was still alive during&nbsp;
this whole chunk. And turns out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.860 --> 00:13:00.360
Maul still had the Darksaber, so now&nbsp;
our Mandalorian Sabine Wren claims it.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.420
Remember Mandalore was liberated by the&nbsp;
Republic at the end of the Clone Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.700
but immediately the Republic became the Empire,&nbsp;
so Mandalore has been under imperial rule. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.000
Sabine goes home like "Yo Mom, it's time&nbsp;
to liberate Mandalore!" "Did someone say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.020
'Liberate Mandalore?'" Yeah Bo-Katan&nbsp;
is obviously in. So young Sabine Wren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.300
with the Darksaber, leads her&nbsp;
people to kick out the Empire!

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:21.600
But Sabine doesn't want to stay here and&nbsp;
rule Mandalore, she's got to go back off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:25.140
with the rebel friends the Ghost Crew.&nbsp;
So she passes the Darksaber to Bo-Katan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:29.640
who has successfully liberated Mandalore...&nbsp;
again. But as we'll find out in The Mandalorian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.380
it doesn't last. Now our rebels, Phoenix Squadron,&nbsp;
has been outsmarting the Empire across the galaxy.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:40.740
So now the Empire brings out the big guns, Grand&nbsp;
Admiral Thrawn! Yes the main villain from the old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:45.120
Star Wars novels, before there were any prequels&nbsp;
or sequels. The story is just part of "Legends"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.800
now, but Thrawn himself is officially canon!&nbsp;
And Thrawn is a real interesting character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.920
very soft spoken, always calm&nbsp;
and collected. Most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.180
he is a genius tactician who instantly sees&nbsp;
through all our rebels' tricks. Every time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:01.440
they escape this season is because he lets them,&nbsp;
he's trying to figure out where the rebel base is.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.160
But the rebels have an advantage, a spy&nbsp;
on the inside, and pretty soon Ghost Crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:09.000
discovers it's their old enemy, Agent Kallus!&nbsp;
Yeah there was an episode where Kallus and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.000
Zeb crash landed on a planet, had to&nbsp;
work together to survive. And Kallus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.300
turns out, is an honorable dude,&nbsp;
who now realizes the Empire is bad.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:19.680
But unfortunately Thrawn found out he's the&nbsp;
spy, and used his broadcasts to pinpoint the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:24.120
rebel base! So Thrawn rolls up in force,&nbsp;
ready to crush the rebellion completely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:28.800
"I am not accepting surrenders at this time." But&nbsp;
there's one thing Thrawn couldn't have predicted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.580
the old creature Bendu, who doesn't&nbsp;
appreciate all this fighting on his planet.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:36.720
So Phoenix Squadron joins the rest of the&nbsp;
rebellion, which has set up shop on Yavin 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:41.700
yeah the planet from A New Hope! They're hanging&nbsp;
out with rebel leader Mon Mothma, the rebellion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:46.200
has reached its final form. But our Ghost Crew&nbsp;
of course was not in A New Hope. They go back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.640
their old stomping grounds Lothal, to stop Thrawn&nbsp;
from building his new improved Tie Defenders.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:55.680
Now Kanan Jarrus makes a big life decision,&nbsp;
it's time to lose the ponytail! Although,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.620
not sure if they should let the blind&nbsp;
guy cut his own hair. Now all series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:02.460
long it's been kind of assumed that Kanan&nbsp;
and Hera are in a romantic relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:07.320
but it's never been mentioned or really shown.&nbsp;
But finally it's confirmed, there was never any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:10.920
doubt, and the understated-ness of their&nbsp;
relationship makes it kind of beautiful.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:15.960
But tragically just then the mission goes bad, and&nbsp;
Kanan got to use the Force to stop the explosion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:22.620
And this is it, there's no other way, Kanan Jarrus&nbsp;
sacrifices himself to save his family! Oh so sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:26.940
for what is mostly a kid's show. Now Ezra Bridger&nbsp;
has always had a strong connection to animals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.240
specifically the wildlife of Lothal&nbsp;
like the super cute loth cats.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.500
But now the mysterious loth wolves show up who&nbsp;
have a mystical connection to the Force. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:38.280
show Ezra the secret back door to the Jedi&nbsp;
Temple, which is a trippy weird space with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:44.160
doorways to different points in space and time!&nbsp;
Ezra finds one that leads to the Asoka Vader duel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.880
and just as Vader is about to win,&nbsp;
woah! He yoinks her out of there.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.460
She's like "Wow man, thanks, I&nbsp;
didn't know the Force could time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:53.160
travel." And she helps him understand&nbsp;
that he can't save Kanan the same way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:56.520
because it would create a time paradox. In&nbsp;
fact she goes back to the time she came from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.280
to I guess lay low for a few&nbsp;
years to not upset the timeline.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:03.360
So now it's time to liberate Lothal! Our&nbsp;
rebels are vastly outnumbered, but Ezra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:09.420
gets reinforcements from the loth wolves! Oh yeah!&nbsp;
These things are beasts. Unfortunately just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:14.400
Thrawn comes back, and he is accepting surrenders&nbsp;
this time. And Ezra's brought in for a Skype call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:19.560
with... Emperor Palpatine himself! He really wants&nbsp;
that Jedi temple time travel, so he's brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:23.280
a piece of it here and tries to tempt Ezra into&nbsp;
opening it by showing him visions of his parents.

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:27.540
But Ezra's come to terms with their loss,&nbsp;
and so he destroys the temple so Palpatine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:31.980
can't get it. Of course there's still Thrawn to&nbsp;
deal with, but Ezra had a secret plan that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:37.020
Thrawn couldn't have predicted. In a pretty early&nbsp;
episode we met a real crazy animal, the Purrgil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:41.700
that are these whale squid things that live&nbsp;
in space and can travel through lightspeed.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:47.520
Ezra, naturally, formed a bond with them, and now&nbsp;
he's summoned them here! Oh! An army of Purrgil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:52.200
taking out all the imperial ships! Not sure if&nbsp;
these things are cute, or eldritch horrors. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:56.280
hold Thrawn here as they grab the whole ship,&nbsp;
Ezra's like "Yo guys, sorry, this was the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:01.500
way." Because Ezra is taking Thrawn off the board,&nbsp;
by warping them out of here, to who knows where.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.920
No one's quite sure what to do with this&nbsp;
development, except of course Chopper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.700
who takes the opportunity to blow up&nbsp;
the entire imperial base. And so our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:12.540
rebels have saved Lothal! And a short&nbsp;
time later, Luke Skywalker blows up two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:16.920
Death Stars and defeats the Emperor, so all&nbsp;
around the galaxy that day is saved. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:22.140
epilogue we learn that Hera was pregnant!&nbsp;
Yes her and Kanan's son, Jacen Syndulla.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.500
But as for Ezra, he left them a message that&nbsp;
he wasn't gone for good, they just need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:29.820
find him. So Sabine Wren is going to take point&nbsp;
on finding him, and she gets help from Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:35.280
Tano! Who's now come back as Ahsoka the White. And&nbsp;
that's where Star Wars Rebels comes to an end.
 &nbsp;

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:41.340
If you like this recap, hit that subscribe button&nbsp;
for more of the best recaps of TV and movies.

